(7584803, 1219676, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Great lighting, details and tones in this photo! Love the pose of the musician as he plays the saxophone. The curves of the instrument undulatea -it moves in a serpentine motion. The air travels the twisting path as the notes emerge not as a hiss but the smooth sounds of some soul jazz. Not sure of the backdrop as that it makes the imagery a little busy with all the lines. The other small critique I have is that a closer crop would have the musician and that smooth music literally filling the frame - a tight crop just above the waist and just a touch more off the top of the frame. That aside this is a great portrait!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Great lighting, details and tones in this photo! Love the pose of the musician as he plays the saxophone. The curves of the instrument undulatea -it moves in a serpentine motion. The air travels the twisting path as the notes emerge not as a hiss but the smooth sounds of some soul jazz. Not sure of the backdrop as that it makes the imagery a little busy with all the lines. The other small critique I have is that a closer crop would have the musician and that smooth music literally filling the frame - a tight crop just above the waist and just a touch more off the top of the frame. That aside this is a great portrait!', '2018-07-22 22:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7584804, 1220656, 68504, '<td valign="top">nutty person.</td>', 'nutty person.', '2018-07-22 22:46:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7584807, 1220319, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Those textures and shapes that weave and undulate in the soil/sand are mesmerizing to look at. B&amp;W was a good choice to showcase those patterns in the ground. As a good shot it needs just a little more...''something'' to push it into the spectacular category. One thing that I see that can help boast a bit more visual interest is to tilt and crop the composition. There is a ''main'' path of rivulets that if you tilt it to the left it could run at a diagonal across the frame. Those dark rivulets ad the bottom are just going straight up but if you tilt it say 35 degrees to the left then some of those nice dark rivulets will appear to pour forth from the bottom right corner. The top area where there it is lighter would also tilt and either be in or pointed towards the top left corner. With that tilt and crop those rivulets then travel from dark to light at a diagonal across the frame.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Those textures and shapes that weave and undulate in the soil/sand are mesmerizing to look at. B&W was a good choice to showcase those patterns in the ground. As a good shot it needs just a little more...''something'' to push it into the spectacular category. One thing that I see that can help boast a bit more visual interest is to tilt and crop the composition. There is a ''main'' path of rivulets that if you tilt it to the left it could run at a diagonal across the frame. Those dark rivulets ad the bottom are just going straight up but if you tilt it say 35 degrees to the left then some of those nice dark rivulets will appear to pour forth from the bottom right corner. The top area where there it is lighter would also tilt and either be in or pointed towards the top left corner. With that tilt and crop those rivulets then travel from dark to light at a diagonal across the frame.', '2018-07-22 22:52:21.000000', NULL, 1),
